  ('78b70bcf-cd82-57df-86d8-2afb314707bc', '7d8a4645-364c-5d6f-90cc-1bebc2ffd0f7', 'Army', 'enlisted', '11Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major — Special assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 11Z (Infantry senior sergeant/sergeant', 'MOS 11Z SGMs serve in special assignments in Inspector General and Equal Opportunity positions. These positions are DA select and the NCOs levied are required to meet specific prerequisites. MOS 11Zs may be assigned special duties at echelons above brigade that are not documented on requirements documents for MOS 11Z (e.g. Senior Enlisted Advisors, Aides to Senior CSMs, etc.). These Soldiers are selected due to their unique qualifications, skills, and prior exceptional performance. These NCOS should be considered highly qualified and not discriminated against due to MOS mismatches on evaluation reports.
